{
  "requirement": "Each bundled skill MUST open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. Each bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, is a site:\n\n:::{sites} skills\n```yaml\nlanguage: markdown\npaths: [assets/skills]\nrule:\n  kind: minus_metadata\nmatch:\n  - \"---\\nname: example\\n---\\n\\n# Example\\n\"\nno_match:\n  - \"# Example\\n\"\n```\n:::",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Site query `skills`.** Running `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow/skills` returned five files:\n- `assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-refactor/SKILL.md`\n\nThese are exactly the five skill directories under `assets/skills`, and the same five names appear in the `SKILLS` constant in `tests/authoring_cli.rs`. A search for `---` lines under `assets/skills` found front matter only in these five `SKILL.md` files. The `references/*.md` files listed by `skill_files` have no front matter, so the query rightly leaves them out. I found no skill the query misses and nothing outside the requirement's scope that it selects.\n\n**Query snippets.** The `match` snippet has front matter followed by a heading. The `no_match` snippet is the same heading without front matter. Together they show that the query selects on front matter, which is how the text says a skill is recognized.\n\n**Obligation and test.** The requirement says each skill opens, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. `bundled_skills_open_with_their_workflow_as_ordered_steps` in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` loops over all five skills and checks three things:\n- The first `## ` heading in the raw `SKILL.md` is exactly `## Workflow`. This checks \"before any other section\".\n- The `workflow_steps` helper parses `- [ ] N.` steps and finds at least two of them. This checks that the workflow is a list of steps.\n- The step numbers equal `1..=n`. This checks that the steps are ordered and consecutive.\n\nA skill with no workflow makes `workflow_steps` panic, and a skill with a different first section fails the first assertion. Each assertion carries the skill name in its failure message. The test carries the `{test}` reference.\n\n**Gaps.** None found. The `SKILLS` list is hard-coded rather than derived from the directory. A sixth skill would be caught by the site query's own review rather than by this test, and the text does not require this test to do so.",
  "references": "bdd2c44e881310eaa176cac0bc633689971a0bf7aef8b3b2d4d14ac7fe919877",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow"
      ],
      "text": [
        "::::{req} skill_conventions.workflow",
        "Each bundled skill MUST open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. Each bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, is a site:",
        "",
        ":::{sites} skills",
        "```yaml",
        "language: markdown",
        "paths: [assets/skills]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: minus_metadata",
        "match:",
        "  - \"---\\nname: example\\n---\\n\\n# Example\\n\"",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"# Example\\n\"",
        "```",
        ":::",
        "::::"
      ]
    },
